the olympic torch relay continues in  tokyo  but it's largely ceremonial with the  torch bearers only allowed to walk with  the flame for a few meters  the state of emergency in the host city  has seen the relay taken away from  public roads  with no spectators  restrictions are also impacting local  business close to the venues  this fencing club across from the main  stadium has been told to leave its  premises until mid-september  because it's being used by tokyo 2020  bad news for a small business  already struggling with the impact of  the pandemic  with the sports industry already lacking  energy to now be told  there will be no practice area is an  additional blow  from a business perspective it's going  to be a big negative  in all honesty eight days to go until  the games and coronavirus continues to  cause disruption  on thursday the first athlete to test  positive under the organizers watch was  confirmed in tokyo  along with a member of games personnel  and four tokyo 2020 contractors  eight women rugby players from kenya are  also isolating after a positive case on  their flight  and u.s basketball star bradley beale  could miss the games  he's isolating at their camp in the  states with his teammates set to fly out  on monday  the american women's football team is  already in japan getting ready for an  olympics like no other  with no fans at all in the stadium it'll  be really different but  um but we have to like be  we have to like be able to imitate like  fans around us and kind of like that  sort of energy we have to feed off each  other because  we're not going to get that from from  any outside  like audience or anything like that no  fans and the medal ceremonies will look  different too  athletes who win gold silver and bronze  will have to collect and present  themselves with the medals  to reduce the risk of spreading the  virus despite all the complications  countries continue to send their teams  to compete including china  who have assembled their biggest ever  delegation for an olympics  all 431 of their athletes were unveiled  at a special ceremony in beijing  with the game set to begin a week on  friday  david stokes al jazeera
 

